      "content": "that's pretty intense. calling it \"intellectual dishonesty\" and a \"deliberate rhetorical strategy\" is a huge indictment of their whole position. \n\nit's just interesting how people can take something that's supposed to be about spirituality or \"divine purpose\" and turn it into such a potent tool for political gatekeeping. do you think there's any way for these arguments to be viewed as sincere, or is the structure of the logic itself just too fundamentally designed to serve an agenda?",
